WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:11.536
Hi, Welcome to the Quantum Labs of Michel
Devoret and Rob Schoelkopf.

00:00:11.684 --> 00:00:16.453
My name is Florian Carle, I am the manager
of the Yale Quantum Institute and the curator

00:00:16.453 --> 00:00:18.721
of our artist in residence program.

00:00:18.721 --> 00:00:23.752
I developed this program to bring talented
artists to our labs for a year-long residency

00:00:23.752 --> 00:00:27.270
to collaborate with our students and give
the general public a glimpse into quantum

00:00:27.270 --> 00:00:28.605
physics through art.

00:00:28.605 --> 00:00:33.586
The piece you are going to hear tonight is
“Quantum Sound: A Live Performance of Superconductive

00:00:33.586 --> 00:00:39.083
Devices” which was developed by sound artist
Spencer Topel, during his residency in 2019

00:00:39.083 --> 00:00:43.207
in close collaboration with quantum physicists
Luke Burkhart and Kyle Serniak.

00:00:43.207 --> 00:00:50.521
All the sounds you are going to hear tonight
were created using these quantum computers

00:00:50.521 --> 00:00:54.254
prototypes that are behind me, deep inside
their dilution fridge at almost absolute zero.

00:00:54.254 --> 00:00:58.564
They have been using them as physical synthesizers
to produce the piece tonight.

00:00:58.564 --> 00:01:02.337
Without further ado, please enjoy this performance
of “Quantum Sound”.

